# Captured failure transcripts are verbatim records, whitespace included.
#
# `docs/release-evidence/**/a2/*-red.txt` are pytest output captured before a fix, kept so a
# later reader can see the failure the fix was written against rather than a description of
# it. pytest indents continuation lines and leaves trailing spaces on blank ones, so
# `git diff --check` reports several hundred trailing-whitespace warnings across them.
#
# Normalising would edit evidence to silence a linter. Declaring the intent is the honest
# option: these paths are exempt from whitespace checks, and the exemption is scoped to the
# transcripts rather than applied to the tree.
docs/release-evidence/**/a2/*-red.txt -whitespace
